    [CI][BugFix] Pin variantlib commit in release wheel workflow (#18486)
    
    ### What this PR does / why we need it?
    
    The release workflow installed variantlib from unpinned git HEAD, but
    upstream removed the enable-if provider subkey (present at 67a62d53,
    removed at current HEAD 31f4a024). The pyproject.toml still sets
    [variant.providers.ascend] enable-if, so ariantlib make-variant failed
    validation with 'unexpected subkeys: {'enable-if'}'.
    
    Pin variantlib to 67a62d53fb8b5a91334d9632bc7d1546ee67349e in all
    make-variant and generate-index-json steps.
    
    ### Does this PR introduce _any_ user-facing change?
    
    ### How was this patch tested?
    
    - vLLM main:
    https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/commit/8cc9aa5ad350f6f80cf3bebb298d410803ff75a9
    
    Signed-off-by: hfadzxy <starmoon_zhang@163.com>

